<title>JAPAN: ANA crew starts 1-day strike, many flights affected.</title>
<headline>ANA crew starts 1-day strike, many flights affected.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A labour union of All Nippon Airways (ANA), which includes pilots and co-pilots, started a 24 hour-strike on Tuesday, a union spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said the strike, which started at midnight (1500 GMT Monday November 18), would ground 357 local flights or 70 percent of the airline's daily domestic runs.</p>
<p>It would be the first serious strike at Japan's second largest carrier in six-and-a-half years.</p>
<p>The strike is mainly over wage rises and bonuses.</p>
</text>
